# ONNX Runtime 1.29.0 released Linux CPU binaries retain small process-lifetime
# allocations made from their dynamic-loader initialization path. PR #23 CI
# demonstrated 720 bytes / 18 allocations whose allocation stacks all pass
# through dlopen() from D.9 DynamicLibrary::open().
#
# This suppression is intentionally applied only to the isolated
# codec-onnx-runtime CTest process in sanitizer builds. It does not disable
# leak detection and does not suppress allocations made later by CODEC or ONNX
# Runtime unless their allocation stack itself contains dlopen().
leak:dlopen
